x.fr:
Mon script de test, relancé sur le code tel quel : $ bash tests/run_tests.sh Testing TP4 Flask app at http://localhost:5005 GET / -> 200 GET /model/mnist -> 200 GET /model/fashion_mnist -> 200 GET /model/cifar10 -> 200 GET /model/cifar100 -> 200 POST /predict/mnist with blank image -> { "class": 1, "confidence": 0.9634141325950623 } POST /predict/fashion_mnist (expect error if model missing) -> { "error": "model file not found on server" } All tests executed. La page d’accueil liste les modèles : MNIST - available Fashion-MNIST - missing (place model file) CIFAR-10 - missing (place model file) CIFAR-100 - missing (place model file) Les trois fichiers sont pourtant dans app/models/ , mais MODELS_DIR pointe vers models/ . En corrigeant ce chemin, un nouveau problème apparaît (un 7 tracé, envoyé aux quatre modèles) : mnist (200, '{
 "class": 7,
 "confidence": 0.9999961853027344
}
') fashion_mnist (200, '{
 "class": 5,
 "confidence": 10.078102111816406
}
') cifar10 (500, '{
 "error": "pop expected at most 1 argument, got 2"
}
') cifar100 (500, '{
 "error": "pop expected at most 1 argument, got 2"
}
')

